          "code": "      <section class=\"lesson\">\n        <p class=\"eyebrow\">Architecture map</p>\n        <h2>Know which layer you are reading</h2>\n        <p>AQLER Timesheet crosses four layers. When code is confusing, first identify which layer owns the current job.</p>\n        <div class=\"architecture-map\">\n          <article><h3>React interface</h3><p>Components, JSX, state, effects, buttons, forms, and visible messages.</p></article>\n          <article><h3>Supabase client</h3><p>Browser requests for Auth and permitted database operations.</p></article>\n          <article><h3>Postgres</h3><p>Tables, durable rows, relationships, constraints, GRANT, and RLS.</p></article>\n          <article><h3>Server automation</h3><p>Cron invokes an Edge Function, which safely uses secrets and calls Brevo.</p></article>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"flow\" aria-label=\"Complete system flow\"><div>User action</div><div>React handler</div><div>Supabase request</div><div>RLS and constraints</div><div>Result updates state</div><div>React renders</div></div>\n      </section>\n",
