          "startLine": 227,
          "endLine": 239,
          "code": "// One completed work-session row returned by the admin reporting view\n{\n  id: 'log-uuid',\n  user_id: 'employee-uuid',\n  shift_date: '2026-08-24',\n  time_in: '2026-08-24T00:03:00.000Z',\n  time_out: '2026-08-24T09:02:00.000Z',\n  full_name: 'Glenda Cruz',\n  email: 'glenda@aqler.tech'\n}</code></pre></div>\n        <p>The <code>admin_work_logs</code> database view puts log and profile fields into one flat, searchable result. React can request a page of rows without first downloading every profile and log. The relationship and combined search text are prepared in Postgres, not by the browser.</p>\n      </section>\n",
