          "code": "      <section class=\"lesson\">\n        <p class=\"eyebrow\">Syntax decoder</p>\n        <h2>How to read the repeated patterns</h2>\n        <div class=\"cards\">\n          <article class=\"card\"><h3>React state</h3><div class=\"code-wrap\"><pre><code>const [logs, setLogs] = useState([])</code></pre></div><p><code>logs</code> is the current array. <code>setLogs</code> changes it and requests another render. <code>[]</code> is its first value.</p></article>\n          <article class=\"card\"><h3>Arrow callback</h3><div class=\"code-wrap\"><pre><code>onClick={() =&gt; cancelReminder(item.id)}</code></pre></div><p>React stores this unnamed function and calls it after a click. The wrapper lets it pass <code>item.id</code> later instead of calling immediately.</p></article>\n          <article class=\"card\"><h3>Optional chaining</h3><div class=\"code-wrap\"><pre><code>log.profiles?.full_name</code></pre></div><p>Read <code>full_name</code> only if <code>profiles</code> exists. Otherwise the result is <code>undefined</code> rather than an error.</p></article>\n          <article class=\"card\"><h3>Object spread</h3><div class=\"code-wrap\"><pre><code>{ ...current, userId: event.target.value }</code></pre></div><p>Copy every old property, then replace only <code>userId</code> with the new input value.</p></article>\n          <article class=\"card\"><h3>Destructuring</h3><div class=\"code-wrap\"><pre><code>const { data, error } = await query</code></pre></div><p>Wait for the query result object, then create local variables from its <code>data</code> and <code>error</code> properties.</p></article>\n          <article class=\"card\"><h3>Query chain</h3><div class=\"code-wrap\"><pre><code>supabase\n  .from('logs')\n  .select('*')\n  .eq('user_id', user.id)\n  .order('created_at', { ascending: false })</code></pre></div><p>Choose <code>logs</code>, request columns, keep this employee’s rows, and return newest rows first. The chain forms one request.</p></article>",
