          "code": "      <section class=\"lesson module-section\" id=\"navbar\">\n        <div class=\"module-heading\"><span class=\"card-number\">3</span><div><h2>Shared navigation</h2><p>Displays identity, role-specific links, responsive layout, and sign out.</p></div></div>\n        <ul class=\"file-list\"><li><code>src/components/Navbar.jsx</code></li></ul>\n        <div class=\"module-tabs\" role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Navbar views\"><button class=\"module-tab\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\" data-panel=\"nav-overall\">Overall</button><button class=\"module-tab\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-panel=\"nav-code\">Code chunks</button><button class=\"module-tab\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-panel=\"nav-logic\">Logical explanation</button></div>\n        <div class=\"module-panel\" id=\"nav-overall\" role=\"tabpanel\"><p>The parent page supplies <code>user</code>, <code>onSignOut</code>, and <code>isAdmin</code> as props. The component does not load data itself. It renders the same reusable header on Home and Admin.</p></div>\n        <div class=\"module-panel\" id=\"nav-code\" role=\"tabpanel\" hidden>\n          <div class=\"code-wrap\"><pre><code>{isAdmin &amp;&amp; (\n  &lt;Link to=\"/admin\"&gt;Employee Logs&lt;/Link&gt;\n)}</code></pre></div><p>The admin link exists only when the prop is true.</p>\n          <div class=\"code-wrap\"><pre><code>&lt;p className=\"max-w-40 truncate md:max-w-none\"&gt;\n  {user.email}\n&lt;/p&gt;</code></pre></div><p>Small screens limit and truncate the email. At the medium breakpoint, the width restriction is removed.</p>\n          <div class=\"code-wrap\"><pre><code>&lt;button onClick={onSignOut}&gt;Sign Out&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre></div><p>React stores the function for the future click; it does not call it during render.</p>\n        </div>",
