          "code": "      <section class=\"lesson module-section\" id=\"utilities\">\n        <div class=\"module-heading\"><span class=\"card-number\">4</span><div><h2>Shared layouts and application utilities</h2><p>Provides the administrator page frame and makes theme/PWA actions available across pages without repeating the same logic.</p></div></div>\n        <ul class=\"file-list\"><li><code>src/pages/AdminLayout.jsx</code></li><li><code>src/components/PublicUtilities.jsx</code></li><li><code>src/context/AppUtilitiesContext.jsx</code></li><li><code>src/context/appUtilities.js</code></li></ul>\n        <div class=\"module-tabs\" role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Shared utility views\"><button class=\"module-tab\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\" data-panel=\"utilities-overall\">Overall</button><button class=\"module-tab\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-panel=\"utilities-code\">Code chunks</button><button class=\"module-tab\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-panel=\"utilities-logic\">Logical explanation</button></div>\n        <div class=\"module-panel\" id=\"utilities-overall\" role=\"tabpanel\"><p><code>AppUtilitiesContext</code> owns values that several unrelated pages need, including the selected theme and the browser’s install event. <code>PublicUtilities</code> turns those values into visible controls. <code>AdminLayout</code> provides one consistent administrator header and content boundary, then renders each admin page inside its <code>children</code> position.</p><div class=\"flow\"><div>Provider stores shared state</div><div>Context exposes values/actions</div><div>Utility controls consume context</div><div>AdminLayout receives page content</div><div>Shared interface renders</div></div></div>\n        <div class=\"module-panel\" id=\"utilities-code\" role=\"tabpanel\" hidden><p>The complete provider, context helper, utility controls, and administrator layout load here as notebook cells.</p></div>\n        <div class=\"module-panel\" id=\"utilities-logic\" role=\"tabpanel\" hidden><ol class=\"logic-steps\"><li><strong>The provider wraps the application.</strong><span>Its state remains available while users move between routes.</span></li><li><strong>Child components call the context hook.</strong><span>They receive the same theme and installation actions without long prop chains.</span></li><li><strong>PublicUtilities renders global controls.</strong><span>The control calls the action supplied by context.</span></li><li><strong>AdminLayout receives children.</strong><span>Each administrator module supplies its unique content inside the shared frame.</span></li></ol></div>\n      </section>\n",
