          "code": "const { error, data } = await supabase\n  .from('logs')\n  .insert({ user_id: user.id, time_in: now.toISOString() })\n  .select()\n  .single()</code></pre></div>\n          <h3>Calculate Time Out duration</h3><div class=\"code-wrap\"><pre><code>const savedTimeIn = new Date(savedSession.time_in)\nconst hours = ((now - savedTimeIn) / (1000 * 60 * 60)).toFixed(2)</code></pre></div><p>Subtracting Date values returns milliseconds. Dividing converts milliseconds to hours.</p>\n          <h3>Disable impossible buttons</h3><div class=\"code-wrap\"><pre><code>disabled={isLoading || !!activeTimeIn}\ndisabled={isLoading || !activeTimeIn}</code></pre></div><p>Time In is disabled during loading or an active session. Time Out is disabled when there is no active session.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"module-panel\" id=\"time-logic\" role=\"tabpanel\" hidden><ol class=\"logic-steps\"><li><strong>Home loads the employee’s logs.</strong><span><code>user_id</code> filters the query; RLS independently enforces ownership.</span></li><li><strong>Home finds the unfinished row.</strong><span>A null <code>time_out</code> means the session is still open.</span></li><li><strong>Time In checks state and the processing ref.</strong><span>The guard blocks an already-open session and rapid duplicate clicks.</span></li><li><strong>One log row is inserted.</strong><span>It contains <code>time_in</code>; its null <code>time_out</code> makes it active. React prepends the returned row.</span></li><li><strong>Time Out uses the same processing ref as a lock.</strong><span>It blocks another click without waiting for a render.</span></li><li><strong>The same row receives <code>time_out</code>.</strong><span>The query matches its ID, employee ID, and still-null Time Out so a completed row cannot be completed twice.</span></li><li><strong>React replaces the old row with the returned completed row.</strong><span><code>activeSession</code> becomes null and the controls return to Time In.</span></li></ol></div>\n      </section>\n",
