          "code": "link.remove()\nURL.revokeObjectURL(url)</code></pre></div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"module-panel\" id=\"admin-logic\" role=\"tabpanel\" hidden><ol class=\"logic-steps\"><li><strong>The setup effect loads profiles and active reminders once.</strong><span><code>Promise.all</code> starts both independent queries together. Logs have their own effect because their page and search change more often.</span></li><li><strong>Typing changes immediate <code>search</code> state.</strong><span>The debounce cleanup cancels abandoned timers; a 400 ms pause copies the trimmed text into <code>debouncedSearch</code> and resets page 1.</span></li><li><strong>The log effect sends a server query.</strong><span>Its dependency array is <code>[page, debouncedSearch, refreshNumber]</code>, so page buttons, a settled search, or Refresh cause a new request.</span></li><li><strong>Postgres searches the flat reporting view.</strong><span>The view exposes name, email, date, and log information through <code>search_text</code>; <code>ilike</code> filters before rows reach the browser.</span></li><li><strong>The response contains rows plus a count.</strong><span><code>range</code> returns one page, while the exact total calculates <code>totalPages</code>.</span></li><li><strong>Export sends separate batched queries.</strong><span>It deliberately gathers every current search match rather than exporting only the visible page.</span></li><li><strong>The rows become CSV and a Blob URL.</strong><span>Quotes are escaped, a temporary anchor is clicked automatically, then the anchor and URL are removed from browser memory.</span></li></ol></div>\n      </section>\n",
