          "code": "      <section class=\"lesson module-section\" id=\"processor\">\n        <div class=\"module-heading\"><span class=\"card-number\">8</span><div><h2>Scheduled email Edge Function</h2><p>Checks due schedules, claims each one once per local date, and calls Brevo.</p></div></div>\n        <ul class=\"file-list\"><li><code>supabase/functions/process-email-reminders/index.ts</code></li></ul>\n        <div class=\"module-tabs\" role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Email processor views\"><button class=\"module-tab\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\" data-panel=\"proc-overall\">Overall</button><button class=\"module-tab\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-panel=\"proc-code\">Code chunks</button><button class=\"module-tab\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-panel=\"proc-logic\">Logical explanation</button></div>\n        <div class=\"module-panel\" id=\"proc-overall\" role=\"tabpanel\"><p>The function is an HTTP worker. A Supabase Cron job must POST to it regularly. It uses the service-role key on the server, loads up to 50 active reminders, evaluates each schedule in its timezone, prevents duplicate same-day sends, and sends through Brevo.</p><aside class=\"callout warning\"><strong>Important</strong>Creating an Edge Function does not automatically schedule it. A Cron job or other caller must invoke the endpoint.</aside></div>\n        <div class=\"module-panel\" id=\"proc-code\" role=\"tabpanel\" hidden>\n          <h3>Load active work</h3><div class=\"code-wrap\"><pre><code>const { data: schedules, error } = await supabase\n  .from('email_reminders')\n  .select('id, subject, message, days_of_week, reminder_time, timezone, last_sent_on, profiles(email, full_name)')\n  .eq('status', 'active')\n  .limit(50)</code></pre></div>\n          <h3>Skip schedules that are not due</h3><div class=\"code-wrap\"><pre><code>if (",
