          "startLine": 701,
          "endLine": 714,
          "code": "      <section class=\"lesson module-section\" id=\"shifts\">\n        <div class=\"module-heading\"><span class=\"card-number\">9</span><div><h2>Shift schedules and date overrides</h2><p>Combines a repeating weekly baseline with exceptions for exact calendar dates.</p></div></div>\n        <ul class=\"file-list\"><li><code>src/pages/Shift.jsx</code></li><li><code>src/components/shifts/ShiftHeader.jsx</code></li><li><code>src/components/shifts/BaselineScheduleEditor.jsx</code></li><li><code>src/components/shifts/WeekScheduleEditor.jsx</code></li><li><code>src/lib/shiftSchedule.js</code></li><li><code>docs/modules/SHIFT_SCHEMA.sql</code></li></ul>\n        <div class=\"module-tabs\" role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Shift schedule views\"><button class=\"module-tab\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\" data-panel=\"shift-overall\">Overall</button><button class=\"module-tab\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-panel=\"shift-code\">Code chunks</button><button class=\"module-tab\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-panel=\"shift-logic\">Logical explanation</button></div>\n        <div class=\"module-panel\" id=\"shift-overall\" role=\"tabpanel\">\n          <p><code>shifts</code> stores the employee’s normal repeating weekday pattern. <code>shift_overrides</code> stores only dates that differ from that pattern. The page loads both tables and builds one effective seven-day view by checking the exact date first and the weekday baseline second.</p>\n          <div class=\"flow\" aria-label=\"Shift schedule priority\"><div>Displayed date</div><div>Find exact-date override</div><div>Override found: use custom time or day off</div><div>No override: find weekday baseline</div><div>Render effective shift</div></div>\n          <div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Admin choice</th><th>Database action</th><th>Meaning when displayed</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n            <tr><td>Recurring working day</td><td>Upsert one <code>shifts</code> row using employee plus weekday.</td><td>This time repeats every matching weekday.</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Recurring day off</td><td>Delete that weekday’s <code>shifts</code> row.</td><td>A missing baseline row means the employee normally has that day off.</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Custom time</td><td>Upsert one <code>shift_overrides</code> row using employee plus exact date.</td><td>That date uses the custom hours instead of the baseline.</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Date-specific day off</td><td>Upsert an override with null times and <code>is_day_off = true</code>.</td><td>Only that calendar date becomes a day off.</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Use baseline</td><td>Delete the exact-date override.</td><td>The page falls back to the normal weekday row again.</td></tr>\n          </tbody></table></div>",
