          "code": "      <section class=\"lesson module-section\" id=\"database\">\n        <div class=\"module-heading\"><span class=\"card-number\">10</span><div><h2>Database schema, relationships, and RLS</h2><p>Defines durable data, automatic profiles, admin access, and recurring schedules.</p></div></div>\n        <ul class=\"file-list\"><li><code>supabase/migrations/20260813181500_create_timesheet_schema.sql</code></li><li><code>...190000_add_admin_access.sql</code></li><li><code>...193000_link_logs_to_profiles.sql</code></li><li><code>...200000_add_email_reminders.sql</code></li><li><code>...203000_make_reminders_recurring.sql</code></li><li><code>...210000_remove_cancelled_reminders.sql</code></li></ul>\n        <div class=\"module-tabs\" role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Database views\"><button class=\"module-tab\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\" data-panel=\"db-overall\">Overall</button><button class=\"module-tab\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-panel=\"db-code\">Code chunks</button><button class=\"module-tab\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-panel=\"db-logic\">Logical explanation</button></div>\n        <div class=\"module-panel\" id=\"db-overall\" role=\"tabpanel\"><p>The current application treats each <code>logs</code> row as one work session: null <code>time_out</code> means open, and a timestamp means complete. <code>admin_work_logs</code> is the flat reporting/search view used by server-side pagination. <code>profiles</code> mirrors display information from Auth, while schedule and reminder tables store their respective rules. The earliest migration still contains the older <code>active_sessions</code> structure for migration history, but the current React timekeeping flow no longer queries it. Foreign keys create relationships, constraints protect valid data, GRANT opens operations to the authenticated database role, and RLS narrows them per user.</p></div>\n        <div class=\"module-panel\" id=\"db-code\" role=\"tabpanel\" hidden>\n          <h3>Allow one open log row per employee</h3><div class=\"code-wrap\"><pre><code>create unique index if not exists one_open_log_per_user\n  on public.logs (user_id)\n  where time_out is null;</code></pre></div>\n          <h3>Create a profile after Auth changes</h3><div class=\"code-wrap\"><pre><code>create trigger on_auth_user_created\n  after insert or update of email, raw_user_meta_data on auth.users\n  for each row execute procedure public.handle_new_user();</code></pre></div>\n          <h3>Employee and admin SELECT policies</h3><div class=\"code-wrap\"><pre><code>using ((select auth.uid()) = user_id)\n",
