          "code": "      <section class=\"lesson module-section\" id=\"styling\">\n        <div class=\"module-heading\"><span class=\"card-number\">11</span><div><h2>Global styling</h2><p>Defines the active Tailwind theme and identifies which stylesheet is currently connected to the app.</p></div></div>\n        <ul class=\"file-list\"><li><code>postcss.config.js</code></li><li><code>tailwind.config.js</code></li><li><code>src/index.css</code></li><li><code>src/App.css</code></li></ul>\n        <div class=\"module-tabs\" role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Styling views\"><button class=\"module-tab\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\" data-panel=\"style-overall\">Overall</button><button class=\"module-tab\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-panel=\"style-code\">Code chunks</button><button class=\"module-tab\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-panel=\"style-logic\">Logical explanation</button></div>\n        <div class=\"module-panel\" id=\"style-overall\" role=\"tabpanel\"><p><code>postcss.config.js</code> activates Tailwind’s PostCSS plugin and Autoprefixer. <code>tailwind.config.js</code> declares the files Tailwind scans and the project colors. <code>index.css</code> is imported by <code>main.jsx</code>, so its Tailwind import, theme tokens, and body rules apply globally. Most layout styling is written directly as Tailwind classes in JSX. <code>App.css</code> contains CSS but is not imported by the current startup path, so those rules are currently inactive.</p></div>\n        <div class=\"module-panel\" id=\"style-code\" role=\"tabpanel\" hidden>\n          <h3>Load Tailwind and define theme colors</h3><div class=\"code-wrap\"><pre><code>@import \"tailwindcss\";\n",
