          "startLine": 795,
          "endLine": 803,
          "code": "      <section class=\"lesson module-section\" id=\"pwa\">\n        <div class=\"module-heading\"><span class=\"card-number\">14</span><div><h2>PWA installation and offline application shell</h2><p>Explains how the website becomes installable, launches like an app, and retains a cached shell when the network is unavailable.</p></div></div>\n        <ul class=\"file-list\"><li><code>index.html</code></li><li><code>src/main.jsx</code></li><li><code>src/components/PwaInstallHelp.jsx</code></li><li><code>public/manifest.webmanifest</code></li><li><code>public/sw.js</code></li><li><code>public/pwa-icon.svg</code></li><li><code>scripts/generate-pwa-icons.mjs</code></li><li><code>public/pwa-192.png</code> and <code>public/pwa-512.png</code> (binary outputs)</li></ul>\n        <div class=\"module-tabs\" role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"PWA views\"><button class=\"module-tab\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\" data-panel=\"pwa-overall\">Overall</button><button class=\"module-tab\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-panel=\"pwa-code\">Code chunks</button><button class=\"module-tab\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-panel=\"pwa-logic\">Logical explanation</button></div>\n        <div class=\"module-panel\" id=\"pwa-overall\" role=\"tabpanel\"><p>The manifest describes the installed application’s name, start address, colors, display mode, and icons. <code>index.html</code> links that manifest. In production, <code>main.jsx</code> registers <code>sw.js</code>. The service worker caches the application shell and supplies the cached HTML when navigation cannot reach the network. <code>PwaInstallHelp</code> explains or starts installation from the interface.</p><div class=\"flow\"><div>Browser reads manifest link</div><div>Production app registers worker</div><div>Worker caches app shell</div><div>Browser offers installation</div><div>Installed shortcut opens start_url</div><div>Worker assists offline navigation</div></div><aside class=\"callout warning\"><strong>Development behavior</strong>The registration condition uses <code>import.meta.env.PROD</code>, so <code>npm run dev</code> intentionally does not install this service worker. Test it with a production build served over HTTPS or localhost.</aside></div>\n        <div class=\"module-panel\" id=\"pwa-code\" role=\"tabpanel\" hidden><p>The full manifest, registration, service worker, install-help component, SVG icon, and icon-generation script load here.</p></div>\n        <div class=\"module-panel\" id=\"pwa-logic\" role=\"tabpanel\" hidden><ol class=\"logic-steps\"><li><strong>The HTML points to the manifest.</strong><span>This gives the browser install metadata before React renders.</span></li><li><strong>The production page finishes loading.</strong><span><code>main.jsx</code> asks the browser to register <code>/sw.js</code>.</span></li><li><strong>The worker installs.</strong><span>It opens the named cache and stores the root HTML, manifest, and icons.</span></li><li><strong>The worker activates.</strong><span>Old cache versions are removed and the new worker controls open pages.</span></li><li><strong>A same-origin GET occurs.</strong><span>Navigation tries the network and falls back to cached HTML; static assets try cache before network.</span></li><li><strong>The browser decides installability.</strong><span>A valid manifest, icons, secure origin, and service worker allow an install prompt or browser menu option.</span></li></ol></div>\n      </section>\n",
