          "startLine": 804,
          "endLine": 812,
          "code": "      <section class=\"lesson module-section\" id=\"projectfiles\">\n        <div class=\"module-heading\"><span class=\"card-number\">15</span><div><h2>Assets and project reference files</h2><p>Accounts for the remaining editable text assets and human-facing setup/reference material.</p></div></div>\n        <ul class=\"file-list\"><li><code>.gitignore</code></li><li><code>README.md</code></li><li><code>domains-instructions.txt</code></li><li><code>reqts.txt</code></li><li><code>public/favicon.svg</code></li><li><code>public/icons.svg</code></li><li><code>src/assets/react.svg</code></li><li><code>src/assets/vite.svg</code></li><li><code>docs/assets/ui/admin-dashboard.svg</code></li><li><code>docs/assets/ui/employee-dashboard.svg</code></li><li><code>docs/assets/ui/shift-scheduler.svg</code></li><li><code>docs/modules/SHIFT_MODULE.md</code></li><li><code>docs/modules/SHIFT_MODULE.html</code></li><li><code>src/assets/Aqler White.avif</code> and <code>src/assets/hero.png</code> (binary)</li><li><code>docs/assets/ui/guide-ui-mobile.png</code>, <code>login-desktop.png</code>, <code>login-mobile.png</code>, <code>register-desktop.png</code>, and <code>register-mobile.png</code> (binary)</li></ul>\n        <div class=\"module-tabs\" role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Project file views\"><button class=\"module-tab\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\" data-panel=\"projectfiles-overall\">Overall</button><button class=\"module-tab\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-panel=\"projectfiles-code\">Code chunks</button><button class=\"module-tab\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-panel=\"projectfiles-logic\">Logical explanation</button></div>\n        <div class=\"module-panel\" id=\"projectfiles-overall\" role=\"tabpanel\"><p>These files do not own a React feature, but they still have a purpose. Markdown and text files record setup or design notes. SVG files are readable vector-image source. PNG and AVIF files are binary pictures, so the guide identifies their paths and roles without printing meaningless byte data. <code>package-lock.json</code> is generated by npm to lock dependency versions and is intentionally described rather than taught line by line.</p></div>\n        <div class=\"module-panel\" id=\"projectfiles-code\" role=\"tabpanel\" hidden><p>All editable text references and SVG sources load here. Binary image bytes and the generated dependency lockfile are intentionally not rendered as code.</p></div>\n        <div class=\"module-panel\" id=\"projectfiles-logic\" role=\"tabpanel\" hidden><ol class=\"logic-steps\"><li><strong>Build tools read configuration and dependency metadata.</strong><span>People usually edit package.json and allow npm to regenerate the lockfile.</span></li><li><strong>The browser requests image paths.</strong><span>Vite bundles imported assets while files in public keep their root-relative URLs.</span></li><li><strong>Documentation records decisions.</strong><span>It does not execute inside the timesheet application.</span></li></ol></div>\n      </section>\n",
