          "code": "      <section class=\"lesson\">\n        <p class=\"eyebrow\">Beginner glossary</p>\n        <h2>Terms used throughout the walkthrough</h2>\n        <dl class=\"glossary\">\n          <div><dt>Component</dt><dd>A React function that returns interface markup.</dd></div>\n          <div><dt>Prop</dt><dd>A value or callback a parent passes to a child component.</dd></div>\n          <div><dt>State</dt><dd>Component memory that can trigger another render when changed.</dd></div>\n          <div><dt>Render</dt><dd>React evaluating a component to determine what the screen should show.</dd></div>\n          <div><dt>Effect</dt><dd>Work React runs after rendering, such as loading database data.</dd></div>\n          <div><dt>Ref</dt><dd>A persistent container whose change does not itself cause a render.</dd></div>\n          <div><dt>Async</dt><dd>Work that finishes later, such as a network or database request.</dd></div>\n          <div><dt>Promise</dt><dd>An object representing a future fulfilled value or rejected error.</dd></div>\n          <div><dt>Callback</dt><dd>A function given to other code so that code can call it at the appropriate time.</dd></div>\n          <div><dt>Fulfilled</dt><dd>A Promise state meaning the asynchronous work succeeded and produced a value.</dd></div>",
