              "code": "const employeeIds = profiles.map((profile) => profile.id)",
              "explanation": "Transforms every array item into a new value or JSX element and returns the new array. Syntax used here: => arrow function — Creates a function. Before => are its parameters; after => is the returned expression or braced function body. .map(callback) — Takes an existing list, visits every item once, and builds a new list from the returned results. The new list has the same number of positions. Example: [1, 2].map(number => number * 10) produces [10, 20] without changing [1, 2]."
