          "code": "        <article class=\"logic-card\">\n          <header><b>1</b><strong><code>const</code> stores a returned value</strong></header>\n          <div class=\"code-wrap\"><pre><code>const timer = setTimeout(loadLogs, 400)</code></pre></div>\n          <div class=\"explanation\">\n            <strong>What runs?</strong>\n            <p>\n              JavaScript first calls <code>setTimeout(...)</code>. That call schedules\n              <code>loadLogs</code> and returns a timer ID. Then <code>const timer</code>\n              stores that ID. Declaring <code>const</code> is not what starts the timer;\n              evaluating the function call on its right side starts it.\n            </p>\n          </div>\n        </article>\n",
